{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_architecture_backend_architecture", "label": "Backend Architecture (LF-BackEnd)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_architecture_prisma_orm_decision", "label": "Prisma as the ORM", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "Resolved implementation choices", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Prisma (PrismaService + apps/prisma/schema.prisma) was chosen over the spec's open 'Prisma ORM' suggestion and over TypeORM; migrations run via `prisma migrate deploy` in the API container entrypoint so a deploy is always schema-correct before the process boots."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_clerk_auth_decision", "label": "Clerk as the identity provider", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "Resolved implementation choices", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The spec asked for first-party JWT + refresh tokens; the implementation delegates to Clerk instead, so there are no /auth/register or password routes in the API and every protected route consumes a Clerk-issued JWT. Sign-in/sign-up stay on the Next.js frontends."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_booking_aggregate_naming", "label": "Booking aggregate naming (bookings vs reservation)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "Resolved implementation choices", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The spec's 'reservation' maps onto the pre-existing `bookings` module and table; renaming was rejected as churn, so implementation keeps /bookings paths unless a versioned alias is added later."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_chef_role_rename", "label": "chef role replaces provider", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "Resolved implementation choices", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "E1 migration renamed the provider role to chef; provider_id columns are kept temporarily for compatibility rather than dropped in the same migration."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_booking_lifecycle", "label": "Booking lifecycle state machine", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "Booking lifecycle (target)", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "POST /bookings creates a booking as pending; the only automatic transition wired is pending -> confirmed driven by the Stripe payment_intent.succeeded webhook, because the API must never confirm a booking on the client's word. A failed payment deliberately leaves the booking pending so the client can retry."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_payments_module", "label": "payments module (Connect, CESU, commissions)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "Current module layout", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_architecture_prefinanced_cesu", "label": "Prefinanced CESU settlement", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "CESU and commission debits", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "On a prefinanced CESU payment the funds never transit through the platform: the client pays from the issuer's beneficiary area using the chef's CRCESU number (NAN) and the issuer credits the chef directly. No issuer exposes an API, so nothing is programmatically verifiable and the chef must confirm receipt, with a traced admin override as the escape hatch."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_commission_invoice_facture_b", "label": "Commission invoiced as facture B", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "CESU and commission debits", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Because the commission cannot be withheld at charge time on CESU, it is invoiced as facture B (commission_invoices, LF-COM-<year>-NNNN) and collected by SEPA direct debit. The invoice always precedes the debit \u2014 it is the legal basis the debit collects against \u2014 and a failed debit adds an attempt without cancelling the receivable, so invoice numbers never develop holes."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_sepa_core_clawback_window", "label": "SEPA CORE 8-week clawback window", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "CESU and commission debits", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Stripe supports only the SEPA CORE scheme (not B2B), so a debit stays revocable 'no questions asked' for 8 weeks; that deadline is materialised on commission_debits.clawback_window_ends_at rather than assumed."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_stripe_connect_destination_charge", "label": "Stripe Connect destination charge", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "Payments (implemented)", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A card payment is a Connect destination charge: the platform keeps the commission as application_fee_amount and the chef's connected account receives the rest, so the commission is collected atomically at charge time and never has to be invoiced back."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_stripe_event_log_dedup", "label": "stripe_event_logs webhook de-duplication", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "CESU and commission debits", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Stripe re-delivers events, so stripe_event_logs de-duplicates on processed_at rather than on mere row existence \u2014 a row that was inserted but not finished must still be reprocessed."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_commission_debit_event_routing", "label": "Routing payment_intent events by commission_debits lookup", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "CESU and commission debits", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A payment_intent event is routed to the commission engine or the client flow by looking the intent up in commission_debits \u2014 never by metadata, which a Dispute leaves empty and a Mandate does not carry at all."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_clerkauthguard", "label": "ClerkAuthGuard", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "Authentication", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_architecture_adminguard", "label": "AdminGuard (persisted admin role)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "Authentication", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Admin authority is the persisted UserRole.ADMIN in Postgres, not a Clerk claim, so revoking admin does not depend on token refresh."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_raw_body_signature_verification", "label": "Raw-body webhook signature verification", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "Authentication", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "POST /webhooks/clerk and POST /webhooks/stripe are public but signature-verified against the raw request bytes; a Fastify preParsing hook in main.ts captures them for a fixed path list because a re-serialised JSON body would fail verification."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_health_readiness_checks", "label": "Liveness and readiness checks", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "Health checks", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "GET /health is deliberately dependency-free (liveness) while GET /ready pings Postgres, so an orchestrator can distinguish a dead process from a degraded dependency."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_module_layout", "label": "Current NestJS module layout", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "Current module layout (implemented)", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_architecture_target_module_map", "label": "Target backend module map", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "Target backend modules (from specs)", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_architecture_fiscal_attestations", "label": "Fiscal attestations", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "API surface summary", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_architecture_uncollectable_commission_block", "label": "Uncollectable commission blocks a chef", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "CESU and commission debits", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A chef whose commission cannot be collected stops receiving bookings and payments \u2014 the platform's only leverage once the money has bypassed it entirely."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_architecture_backend_architecture", "target": "docs_spec_backend_spec", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "Guiding specs", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_architecture_backend_architecture", "target": "docs_spec_admin_dashboard_spec", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "Guiding specs", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_architecture_backend_architecture", "target": "docs_revisions_followup_release_register", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "Documentation map", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_architecture_booking_aggregate_naming", "target": "docs_spec_backend_reservation", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "Resolved implementation choices", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_architecture_booking_lifecycle", "target": "docs_spec_backend_reservation_lifecycle", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "Booking lifecycle (target)", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_architecture_booking_lifecycle", "target": "docs_architecture_payments_module", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "Booking lifecycle (target)", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_architecture_clerk_auth_decision", "target": "docs_architecture_clerkauthguard", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "Authentication", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_architecture_adminguard", "target": "docs_architecture_clerkauthguard", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "Authentication", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_architecture_module_layout", "target": "docs_architecture_payments_module", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "Current module layout", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_architecture_payments_module", "target": "docs_architecture_stripe_connect_destination_charge", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "Payments (implemented)", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_architecture_payments_module", "target": "docs_architecture_prefinanced_cesu", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "CESU and commission debits", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_architecture_payments_module", "target": "docs_architecture_fiscal_attestations", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "API surface summary", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_architecture_prefinanced_cesu", "target": "docs_architecture_commission_invoice_facture_b", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "CESU and commission debits", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_architecture_commission_invoice_facture_b", "target": "docs_architecture_sepa_core_clawback_window", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "CESU and commission debits", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_architecture_sepa_core_clawback_window", "target": "docs_architecture_uncollectable_commission_block", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "CESU and commission debits", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_architecture_commission_debit_event_routing", "target": "docs_architecture_stripe_event_log_dedup", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.85, "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "CESU and commission debits", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_architecture_commission_debit_event_routing", "target": "docs_architecture_commission_invoice_facture_b", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "CESU and commission debits", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_architecture_raw_body_signature_verification", "target": "docs_architecture_stripe_event_log_dedup", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.75, "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "Authentication", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_architecture_target_module_map", "target": "docs_spec_backend_module_map", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "Target backend modules (from specs)", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_architecture_target_module_map", "target": "docs_spec_admin_dashboard_spec", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "Admin backlog", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_architecture_payments_module", "target": "docs_spec_backend_payment", "relation": "shares_data_with", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.95, "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "Payments (implemented)", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_architecture_fiscal_attestations", "target": "docs_spec_backend_tax_credit_sap", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.85, "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "API surface summary", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_architecture_chef_role_rename", "target": "docs_spec_backend_roles_permissions", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "Resolved implementation choices", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_architecture_adminguard", "target": "docs_spec_backend_roles_permissions", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.85, "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "Authentication", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_architecture_health_readiness_checks", "target": "docker_compose_postgres_service", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.85, "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "Health checks", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_architecture_uncollectable_commission_block", "target": "agents_clerk_webhook_db_sync", "relation": "semantically_similar_to", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.65, "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "CESU and commission debits", "weight": 1.0}], "hyperedges": [{"id": "cesu_commission_settlement_flow", "label": "CESU payment to commission collection flow", "nodes": ["docs_architecture_prefinanced_cesu", "docs_architecture_commission_invoice_facture_b", "docs_architecture_sepa_core_clawback_window", "docs_architecture_commission_debit_event_routing", "docs_architecture_uncollectable_commission_block"], "relation": "form", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/architecture.md"}]}